# Cores restricted to 64-bit devices.  Listed in CORESETS only by the aarch64
# profiles, so the armv7 ones can never pick them up -- coreset lines are raw
# recipe lines and have no scope column, so exclusion is done by coreset
# membership rather than by a per-line filter.
#
# mame (0.2xx): too heavy for the 32-bit devices (Cortex-A7/A9, Mali-400) --
# they are not powerful enough to run it, so building it for them is waste.
# It is the only core for a long tail of computers and consoles (the Sharp MZ
# and NEC PC families, Loopy, Beena, TRS-80, ...), so the systems gated on
# BR2_PACKAGE_LIBRETRO_MAME in es_systems.yml appear on aarch64 only.
# Expect it to dominate the build time of a drop.
mame libretro-mame https://github.com/libretro/mame.git master YES GENERIC Makefile.libretro .

# dolphin: CMakeLists.txt:235 aborts on any 4-byte-pointer target --
# "You're building on an unsupported platform: 'armv7l' with 4-byte
# pointers" -- so it cannot be in a shared coreset.  CMAKE, unlike the
# GENERIC cores above, so it also needs the profile's CMAKE_EXTRA_ARGS.
dolphin libretro-dolphin https://github.com/libretro/dolphin.git master YES CMAKE Makefile build

# play: PS2.  Its Framework hard-includes <GLES3/gl3.h>, which the ATM7039
# sysroot does not have -- SGX540 is GLES2-only -- and a Cortex-A9 could not
# run PS2 emulation anyway.  Needs NO_FAST_MATH (vendored sqlite #errors on
# it) and the -D flags that select the core over the Qt desktop app; both
# live in coreargs/cores.args.
play libretro-play https://github.com/jpd002/Play-.git master YES CMAKE Makefile build

# azahar: 3DS.  Same repo as the standalone azahar package -- the tree carries
# both frontends and ENABLE_LIBRETRO picks the core (src/citra_libretro,
# PREFIX "" -> azahar_libretro.so in the build dir).  64-bit only: the 3DS
# needs a 64-bit host JIT and the 32-bit devices cannot run it anyway.
azahar libretro-azahar https://github.com/johndoe6345789/azahar_libretro.git master YES CMAKE Makefile build

# The Dreamcast forks.  All three -- upstream flycast (tier4-cmake), flycastvl
# and flycast-xtreme -- build a .so named after TARGET_NAME, which defaults to
# "flycast" in all of them.  dist/ is FLAT and make-drop keys renames on the
# basename, so without overriding TARGET_NAME (in coreargs) the three would
# overwrite each other in dist/ before make-drop ever sees them.
#
# 64-bit only: both forks want ARCH=arm64, and the 32-bit devices (Mali-400
# GLESv2, SGX540) cannot run Dreamcast anyway.  Pinned to the same commits the
# in-tree packages used, so this is the same code that shipped before.
flycastvl libretro-flycastvl https://github.com/libretro/flycast.git master@4a913e063c95d1fae98afc64645831de0bcad57e YES GENERIC Makefile .
flycast-xtreme libretro-flycast-xtreme https://github.com/metallic77/flycast.git master@603814c9f73b773c455d9a497f389d2f93a257fd YES GENERIC Makefile .

# yabasanshiro: Saturn.  Lives on the "yabasanshiro" branch of libretro/yabause,
# and the core builds out of yabause/src/libretro rather than the repo root.
# The in-tree package picked a tuned platform per SoC (arm64_cortex_a53_gles3,
# RK3326, sm8250, ...) but a drop is built once per ABI, so it takes that
# package's own aarch64 fallback -- platform=unix, which is the profile default.
yabasanshiro libretro-yabasanshiro https://github.com/libretro/yabause.git yabasanshiro@39535a6abcad5abf9f71c8b2a7975f005ee12ed6 YES GENERIC Makefile yabause/src/libretro

# panda3ds: 3DS, second core for that system alongside azahar.  CMAKE, and the
# aarch64 branch of the in-tree package disabled CryptoPP's asm and LuaJIT --
# both are x86-only there.  GLES rather than desktop GL, like every other core
# on these profiles.
#
# ENABLED=NO: it has never built here and 3ds is served by azahar, which does.
# Parked rather than deleted -- the recipe, its cmake args in coreargs and its
# cores.symbols row all stay valid, so flip NO -> YES to pick it back up.
panda3ds libretro-panda3ds https://github.com/wheremyfoodat/Panda3DS.git v0.9 NO CMAKE Makefile build
